title: "Bounds for the kissing number in dimension 5, 40 <= kappa(5) <= 44: a Lean 4 formalisation via three-point certificates"
type: software
version: "2"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24145123"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/kissing-number-5"
authors:
  - name: alejandrozarco
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 proof, checked by the Lean kernel, that the kissing number of five-dimensional space is at least 40 and at
  most 44: the 40 roots of D5 for the lower bound, and an exact Bachoc-Vallentin three-point certificate of degree 32
  for 45 points, with a Lean proof of three-point positivity on the sphere S^4 up to degree 16, for the upper bound.
  Version 1 proved the upper bound 45 with a degree-16 certificate. Both bounds are known, and 44 is not the best
  known upper bound: Tomar (2026, preprint) proves 43, with Lean proofs that assume the positivity of zonal kernels
  given by data files; the Lean proof here assumes no such hypothesis and uses only Lean's standard axioms. Not peer
  reviewed. AI-produced by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) under the direction of the repository
  owner and reviewed only by AI models (see AI_DISCLOSURE.md): a machine-checked formalisation of known bounds that
  no human has yet reviewed.
keywords:
  - kissing number
  - D5 root system
  - semidefinite programming
  - three-point bound
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Lean 4
